    "narrative": "Our priority today is capitalizing on the high-upside matchup against Van Eyk and Ure\u00f1a, where the aggregate pitching metrics favor our hitters significantly. **Lawrence Butler** earns our highest confidence rating at 73.47; he is in a prime spot in the two-hole against Ure\u00f1a, benefiting from an elite platoon split and a favorable park factor. Similarly, **Dylan Beavers** (68.38) and **Jeremiah Jackson** (65.32) are must-starts against the suspect Van Eyk, with **Dylan Beavers** seeing a massive boost from the leadoff spot and a 16% park adjustment. **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** remains a staple of the lineup despite facing the tougher Gray, as his elite profile and subtle speed incentives\u2014bolstered by Gray\u2019s slower delivery\u2014maintain his status as a high-floor producer.\n\nWe opted to bench **Yainer Diaz** (52.00) despite a solid projected day, as the difficulty of the Kirby matchup and a more congested schedule forced him to the pine in favor of the higher-efficiency outputs from **Cal Raleigh** and **Will Smith**. **Masyn Winn** (43.38) also just missed the cut; while his stolen base potential is enticing, his current position in the nine-hole combined with a tough pitching environment against Bachar limited his ceiling compared to our starting infielders. We are monitoring **Bryce Harper** and **Luis Arraez** closely, as both face the sharp Henderson (2.97 xERA), which suppresses their ceiling slightly despite their individual pedigree. Managers should keep an eye on weather reports across the board, but with no major storms impacting our core hitters, we are well-positioned to chase gains in the SB category through the aggression of **Dylan Beavers**, **Lawrence Butler**, and **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez**.",
